event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"## 1\n\nI’m really sorry you’re going through this. If you’ve"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" felt this way for months, I completely understand hitting a wall, and you're not crazy for wanting out. \n\nBefore"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" you pull the trigger tomorrow, though—can you take a sick day or a mental health day first? Give yourself "}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"24 hours away from the building just to breathe and think without the immediate pressure of the office around you. Quitting might"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" still be the right move, but it's always better to do it with a clear head rather than in the heat of a brutal"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" week. \n\nEither way, I’m in your corner. Do you want to vent tonight, or do you just want a"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" distraction? Dinner or drinks on me if you’re up for it.\n\n## 2\n\nI understand why people"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" are skeptical of big institutions and CGI, but you don't actually need NASA or satellite imagery to know the Earth is a"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" sphere. People figured this out thousands of years before cameras existed.\n\nFor example, during a lunar eclipse, the Earth"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" passes between the Sun and the Moon, casting its shadow onto the lunar surface. That shadow is always a smooth, curved"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" arc, no matter what time of night the eclipse happens or where the Moon is in the sky. If the Earth were a"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" flat disk, you’d sometimes see an elongated oval or a thin slit depending on the angle. The only shape that casts a circular"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" shadow from every possible direction is a sphere.\n\nOr consider constellations: if you travel from Canada down to Chile, entirely"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" new stars appear above the southern horizon while familiar northern stars sink out of sight. On a flat plane, everyone on Earth would see the exact same"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" stars, just slightly closer or further away. \n\nFaking a digital photo is easy; coordinating millions of independent sailors"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":", airline pilots, surveyors, and amateur stargazers across every continent for thousands of years to maintain a shared illusion is impossible"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":".\n\n## 3\n\nTo understand why the sky is blue, you first have to know two things: sunlight isn't purely"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" white, and the air around us isn't empty space.\n\nLight from the Sun looks white, but it's actually"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" a mix of all the colors of the rainbow combined. Each color travels through space as a wave. Red and orange light travel in long,"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" lazy waves, while blue and violet light travel in short, choppy, energetic waves.\n\nWhen that sunlight hits Earth,"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" it runs into our atmosphere, which is packed with billions of tiny gas molecules—mostly nitrogen and oxygen. \n\nThe long, lazy waves"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" of red and yellow light are big enough to pass right past those tiny molecules without bumping into them much. But the short, choppy blue"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" waves smash directly into the gas particles and bounce off them in every direction. Scientists call this **scattering**. \n\nWhen you"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" look up during the day, you aren't looking at empty space; you’re looking at all those tiny blue"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" waves that got knocked off course, ping-ponging across the entire atmosphere and down into your eyes. \n\n## 4\n\n窗外的"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"雨下得又急又密，敲打在玻璃上，发出细碎而沉闷的声响。路灯昏黄"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"的光晕在被雨水浸湿的柏油路上晕染开来，像融化在水里的油彩。偶尔有车辆"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"飞驰而过，轮胎撕开积水，溅起半人高的水花，转瞬又重归寂静。"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"冷风顺着窗缝渗进屋内，带来泥土与青草混合的微凉潮气。房间里只亮"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"着一盏暖光台灯，在这片朦胧的水汽中，整座城市仿佛都随着这场夜雨，慢慢"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"沉入了深沉的梦乡。\n\n## 5\n\nHi [Name],\n\nThanks so much for putting this together! "}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"\n\nUnfortunately, I won’t be able to make it this Friday—I already have plans lined up for the evening. "}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"\n\nI hope you all have a great time, and I'll catch you at the next one!\n\nBest,  "}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"\n[Your Name]\n\n## 6\n\nMy writing style is clear, adaptable, and grounded, aiming for a balance of rhythm,"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" precision, and substance without leaning on filler or pretense."}}

